<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Kimberley reports 0.6 carat diamond.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Kimberley reports 0.6 carat diamond.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kimberley Diamond Co NL said on Tuesday a diamond weighing 0.6 carats was recovered from the number three pit at its Blina project in Western Australia.</p>
<p>The find takes the number of diamonds recovered to 42, weighing a total of 11.566 carats, it said.</p>
<p>Kimberley, which is carrying out a bulk sampling programme at Blina, earlier this month reported the recovery of a diamond weighing 3.34 carats from its number two pit.</p>
<p>Final processing and observing of all samples is about 30 percent complete, Kimberley said.  </p>
<p>Kimberley said it will release further results from time to time.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
